    "description": "Product Engineer (Transcription) \u2014 Granola\n\nLocation: London\n\nHey! We're team Granola \ud83d\udc4b\n\nWe're looking for an engineer who loves audio and transcription, and loves building products in a fast-paced, iterative environment.\n\nIn this role, you will make Granola the best desktop transcription app that exists. You'll be talking directly with users to understand their transcription problems. You will be part of the founding team and help unlock Granola for the next 100x users.\n\nIn this role, you will:\n\n- Own and build our transcription features end-to-end. Things like:\n\n- Audio capture on macOS and Windows\n\n- Echo cancellation\n\n- Connections to transcription providers/models\n\n- Local transcription models\n\n- Diarisation/attribution\n\n- Transcription UI/UX on our desktop app\n\n- Logging and evals so we know whether all this is working/improving!\n\n- Feel every transcription papercut, because you\u2019ll be using Granola for every meeting!\n\n- Optimise the application for speed, scale, and reliability\n\n- Interact with users to understand their problems and design solutions\n\n- Collaborate with a cross-functional team of engineers, product managers, designers, and other members of the team to create a cutting-edge product\n\nYour background looks something like:\n\n- Experience with audio capture, real-time media pipelines\n\n- Engineering experience at tech and product-driven companies\n\n- Proficiency with TypeScript, Node.js, and React, and ideally Electron\n\n- Comfortable dropping into native code and OS audio APIs (CoreAudio, WASAPI, \u2026) when needed, even if you're not a low-level specialist\n\n- Experience with speech-to-text models/providers\n\nAs a person, you\u2026\n\n- Are first and foremost a builder.\n\n- Are excited to work in-person from our office in London (most of the time)\n\n- Love working in a startup environment (you either have experience working in a startup or are really drawn to the zero-to-one phase)\n\n- Value working with people who are kind, ambitious, and pragmatic\n\n- Have an interest in AI/ML (direct experience not required)\n\n- Thrive in a fast-paced environment with evolving requirements and priorities\n\nAbout the opportunity\n\nWe are living in the most exciting time for tool builders since Engelbart's demo https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mother_of_All_Demos in 1968. We want to assemble the best crew to build this future together, here in London. Our compensation philosoph",
