    "description": "OUR MISSION:\n\nOmnea is the agentic operating system for procurement.\n\nProcurement touches every pound a business spends, yet requests still stall for weeks and approvals get lost in inboxes. Our AI-first platform changes that: our agents capture requests, route approvals, onboard suppliers, flag risk and track every renewal, while anyone in the business can ask a question and get an answer grounded in their own company\u2019s data. Buying becomes painless for everyone, procurement gets a seat at the table, and our customers have saved more than 100,000 hours of manual work so far.\n\nCompanies like Spotify, PayPal, T. Rowe Price, JustEat, Adyen and S&P Global run procurement on Omnea. We\u2019re backed by $75M from Khosla Ventures, Insight Partners and Accel, and we\u2019ve been named the UK\u2019s number one startup in the Startups 100, ranked 11th on Sifted\u2019s 2026 list of Europe\u2019s fastest-growing companies, and recognised as one of Fast Company\u2019s Most Innovative Companies.\n\nTalent density matters more to us than almost anything else. We keep the bar high in every team, so everyone here has real ownership and real impact. Our team is full of former founders and operators who\u2019ve scaled unicorns, and we\u2019re looking for people who want to do the best work of their careers alongside them.\n\nFind out more about the team and life at Omnea here https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLpjeHyocsu3ZoDn3sfODjqIR2L_DW3dgb.\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nAI is changing what it means to deploy enterprise software. Configuring a customer's procurement workflows used to mean weeks of manual setup, integration by integration, edge case by edge case. Increasingly, that first-draft build work can be directed rather than done by hand: AI agents can generate workflow configurations, draft integration mappings, and produce the initial pass on a customer's setup.\n\nThe job shifts with it. Instead of building every workflow yourself, you specify exactly what needs to exist, direct AI to build it, and apply the judgment AI can't: is this the right configuration for this customer's approval policy, will Legal and Finance actually sign off on it, does it hold up once real spend starts flowing through it. In practice, that might mean catching that the approval chain AI just drafted works perfectly for HQ, but misses a regional delegation-of-authority rule that would fail an audit in the customer's APAC entity.\n\nAs Omnea's AI Solu",
