    "description": "About the Team\n\nOpenAI didn\u2019t begin as a traditional company. It began as an idea: that artificial intelligence could be developed in a way that benefits everyone. As a creative team, our role is to help make sure the work behind that idea is understood, as it leaves the lab and meets the world.\n\nThis company works at the frontier of intelligence. Like any frontier, it\u2019s unfinished, constantly shifting, and still being explored. Our job is to stay close to that uncertainty and help shape how this story gets told, in a way that feels grounded and human. We do this through campaigns, launches, films, brand systems, and work that doesn\u2019t fit neatly into any of those categories yet. This team is for people who want to help shape something from the beginning.\n\nThis team is for people who are energized by ambiguity, intellectually curious, and excited to build something enduring from the beginning.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nAs Content Studio Creative Lead, you will build and lead a centralized content studio that serves the broader creative team. You will be both a senior maker and a capability builder: creating timely, high-quality content while shaping the studio\u2019s creative approach, talent network, and quality standards, in partnership with Production on the processes that support the work at scale.\n\nWe\u2019re looking for someone who can move fluidly between hands-on content creation and creative systems thinking. You will work closely with leaders, researchers, creative teams, and external partners to capture stories at the source and turn them into compelling work for web, social, and the broader OpenAI brand.\n\nThis role is based in San Francisco, CA. We use a hybrid work model of 3 days in the office per week and offer relocation assistance to new employees. Travel for production may be required.\n\nIn this role, you will:\n\n- Define the content studio\u2019s creative vision, creative strategy, and measures of quality and effectiveness, and partner with Production on production workflows.\n\n- Identify the right creative talent and partners across internal teams, freelancers, and agencies, working with Production to build the team and production approach around each project.\n\n- Create reusable formats, playbooks, and standards that help teams produce strong work quickly across web, social, editorial, and brand channels.\n\n- Partner with creative leads to prioritize requests and set",
