    "description": "About the Role\n\nDots is looking for a Backend Engineer to build the systems that power our product. You\u2019ll work closely with product, design, and engineering to turn ideas into reliable services and deliver features from design through production.\n\nIn this role, you will:\n\n- Design, build, and maintain backend services and APIs.\n\n- Develop data models and improve database performance.\n\n- Build integrations with third-party services.\n\n- Improve system reliability, security, and observability.\n\n- Write tested, maintainable code and participate in code reviews.\n\n- Investigate production issues and address their root causes.\n\n- Help shape technical decisions as the product grows.\n\nYou might thrive in this role if you have:\n\n- Experience building and operating backend applications in production.\n\n- Strong proficiency in a backend programming language.\n\n- Solid understanding of API design, relational databases, and data modeling.\n\n- Experience with cloud infrastructure, automated testing, and deployment workflows.\n\n- Ability to balance speed with quality and make practical technical decisions.\n\n- Clear communication and a collaborative approach to solving problems.\n\nNice to have:\n\n- Experience with distributed systems, background jobs, and event-driven architectures.\n\n- Familiarity with caching, queues, and performance optimization.\n\n- Experience working on a small team or an early-stage product.\n\nAbout OpenAI\n\nOpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity.\n\nWe are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic.\n\nFor additional information, please see OpenAI\u2019s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement https://cdn.openai.com/policies/eeo-policy-statement.pdf.\n\nBackground checks for appl",
