    "description": "WIRELESS REGULATORY ENGINEER \u2013 SAR\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nThe Consumer Devices team at OpenAI builds products that bring advanced AI capabilities into thoughtfully designed consumer experiences. We work across hardware, software, design, and research to develop reliable products from early exploration through production.\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe\u2019re looking for a Wireless Regulatory Engineer to support RF exposure compliance for consumer hardware. You\u2019ll work closely with RF, antenna, hardware, software, and regulatory teams throughout the product development lifecycle, helping ensure products meet applicable requirements while maintaining a high bar for performance and user experience.\n\nThis role is based in Mountain View, CA. We use a hybrid work model of four days in the office per week and offer relocation assistance to new employees.\n\nIN THIS ROLE, YOU WILL:\n\n- Develop and execute RF exposure test and validation strategies for consumer wireless products.\n\n- Partner with engineering teams to evaluate product designs and identify potential compliance risks throughout development.\n\n- Perform and analyze RF exposure measurements and communicate findings clearly to cross-functional teams.\n\n- Support product development from early prototypes through validation, certification, and production.\n\n- Coordinate testing with external laboratories and review results and supporting documentation.\n\n- Translate applicable regulatory requirements into practical engineering guidance.\n\n- Partner with RF and antenna teams to balance regulatory requirements with product performance.\n\n- Develop tools and workflows that improve testing efficiency, consistency, and data analysis.\n\n- Investigate issues, identify root causes, and work with engineering teams to develop effective solutions.\n\n- Support global regulatory certification activities for wireless consumer products.\n\nYOU MIGHT THRIVE IN THIS ROLE IF YOU:\n\n- Have a Master\u2019s degree or equivalent experience in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, RF Engineering, or a related technical field.\n\n- Bring deep experience with SAR, RF exposure, or wireless regulatory testing.\n\n- Have a strong understanding of RF fundamentals, measurement techniques, and wireless systems.\n\n- Have experience translating regulatory requirements into engineering and product decisions.\n\n- Are comfortable performing hands-on testing, analyzing complex measu",
