    "description": "We're building the future of Speech Intelligence at Speechmatics, and we need someone who can own the technical engine behind how customers discover, adopt, and grow with our platform. This is a hands-on backend engineering role, where your work directly shapes the journey from a customer's first interaction with our website to their first meaningful moment of value. If you thrive shipping, iterating, and making a measurable commercial difference, then we\u2019d love to hear from you. &nbsp;\n\nWhat you'll do &nbsp;\n\nOwn the backend development and ongoing health of the Speechmatics website and self-serve portal\n\nBuild and maintain new custom components from scratch, turning design specifications into reliable, performant, production-ready code\n\nManage Vercel deployments and backend infrastructure, keeping the live site fast, stable, and technically sound\n\nImplement UI design changes end-to-end, bridging the gap between what's designed and what goes live\n\nWrite Python-based queries to surface insights across the self-serve portal and support data-driven decisions across the team\n\nIdentify and act on opportunities to improve conversion across the self-serve funnel through well-timed, well-designed product experiences\n\nCollaborate closely with product, design, and data teams in a cross-functional, async-friendly way, working closely together to remove blockers and unlock opportunities\n\nOwn the ongoing improvement of site performance, loading speed, and technical reliability &nbsp;\n\nWhat you'll need &nbsp;\n\nProficiency in JavaScript and TypeScript for website backend development, with a track record of shipping and maintaining production code\n\nHands-on Python experience, particularly for data queries\n\nDemonstrable experience with LLM and AI-first development workflows, tools like Claude, Cursor, or similar&nbsp;\n\nExperience in a product-led growth or self-serve SaaS environment, with a clear understanding of conversion funnels and how engineering choices affect them\n\nThe ability to operate with significant autonomy, you\u2019ll thrive with ambiguity and finding creative solutions &nbsp;\n\nExceptionally strong communication skills, with a habit of being proactive, transparent, and thorough in async and cross-functional settings\n\nA pragmatic, shipping-first mindset, you default to iterating in production\n\nExperience managing and deploying to platforms like Vercel, or equivale",
